## 🧰 Components Used

The following hardware components are used to develop the Arduino-based vehicle speed detection system:

- **Arduino UNO** – Processes sensor data and calculates vehicle speed.
- **IR Sensors (2)** – Detect the vehicle at two fixed points.
- **16×2 LCD Display with I2C Module** – Displays the measured speed.
- **Buzzer** – Provides an alert when the speed exceeds the predefined limit.
- **Breadboard** – Used to assemble and test the circuit.
- **Jumper Wires** – Connect the components to the Arduino UNO.
- **USB Cable / Power Supply** – Supplies power to the Arduino.
